The ui-dashboard client-to-server join returns nothing, so I'll rely on the preserve and consign evidence I already have. The findings are consistent enough to report: one restarted consign pod, and food-service's slow `save` propagating through preserve-service to the dashboard.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-consign-service",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'ts-consign-service%' ORDER BY time LIMIT 5", "claim": "Consign-service pod ts-consign-service-6cfc6565f6-fphwj shows container restarts = 1 during the abnormal window; normal period has none."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT time, service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name, message FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-consign-service' AND (message LIKE 'Starting %Application%' OR message LIKE 'Started %Application in%') ORDER BY time", "claim": "Consign-service logs a fresh Spring Boot startup at 06:38:19 on a new pod, confirming a restart."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n, min(time) t0, max(time) t1 FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND attr_http_response_status_code=503 GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "ts-ui-dashboard returns 503 for consign account requests only between 06:37:54 and 06:38:36, matching the restart window."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "service": "ts-food-service",
      "fault_kind": "application_method_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95),1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-food-service' AND span_name IN ('FoodOrderRepository.save','Session.merge foodsearch.entity.FoodOrder','Transaction.commit','INSERT ts.food_order') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "FoodOrderRepository.save p95 about 2.1 s, while its merge, commit and INSERT child spans stay at roughly 2-12 ms."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, s.service_name callee, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(c.duration/1e6,0.95),1) client_p95, round(approx_quantile(s.duration/1e6,0.95),1) server_p95 FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.trace_id=c.trace_id AND s.parent_span_id=c.span_id WHERE c.attr_span_kind='Client' AND s.attr_span_kind='Server' AND c.service_name='ts-preserve-service' AND s.service_name='ts-food-service' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Preserve-service calls to food-service take about 2.2 s at p95; the food server span accounts for nearly all of it."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "ts-consign-service", "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95),1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name LIKE '%consignservice%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Dashboard consign-account requests fail with 503 and slow to about 460-590 ms p95 after the consign restart."}]},
    {"from": "ts-food-service", "to": "ts-preserve-service",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95),1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name IN ('POST /api/v1/foodservice/orders','POST /api/v1/preserveservice/preserve') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Food order POSTs are slow at p95 about 2.1 s, and preserve-service's own server spans rise with them."}]},
    {"from": "ts-preserve-service", "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95),1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='POST /api/v1/preserveservice/preserve' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "The user-facing preserve request at ts-ui-dashboard slows to about 1.4 s p95, above the preserve-service server span."}]}
  ]
}
```

